{
  "matches": [
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n1",
        "action:n2"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "To begin the process, Rental Items are Returned to the Store."
      ],
      "justification": "The opening clause establishes the process start and the initial return step, faithfully captured by the init and action elements."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b1->n3",
        "action:n3"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the \"Customer returns the items to the store,\" then we can continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "The conditional structure and its positive arm are accurately modeled with the branch, guard, and action elements."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b1->n4",
        "action:n4"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "However, if the \"Delivery Crew picks-up items at the event site,\" then we also continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "The alternative condition and resulting action match the source exactly."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:nc"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "During this step, the items are counted and compared to the original contract."
      ],
      "justification": "Directly implements the counting and comparison step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b2->n5",
        "action:n5"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the \"Order is complete and all items were returned,\" then we proceed with the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Accurately models the complete-order condition and continuation."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b2->n6",
        "action:n6"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "However, if the \"Order is incomplete and items are missing,\" we still continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Faithfully captures the incomplete-order branch and continuation."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b2->n7",
        "action:n7"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Similarly, if the \"Order is complete but items are damaged,\" we email the customer to inform them of the damage and additional charges."
      ],
      "justification": "Correctly models the damaged-item condition and the corresponding notification action."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b11->n8",
        "action:n8"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "After this, if the \"Items are packed for an existing order,\" we continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Matches the packing condition and continuation step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b11->n9",
        "action:n9"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Alternatively, if the \"Items are stored for future orders,\" we also continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Faithfully captures the storage condition and continuation."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n10"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "In case of missing items and replacement charges, we email the customer to inform them."
      ],
      "justification": "Directly implements the notification step for missing items."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b3->n15",
        "action:n15"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the \"Customer returns the missing items,\" we continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Accurately models the conditional return of missing items."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b3->n16",
        "action:n16"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "However, if the \"Customer does not return the missing items,\" we still continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Faithfully captures the negative return branch and continuation."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n14"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Finally, when the process is complete, it ends."
      ],
      "justification": "Correctly maps the stated process termination."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b6->n13",
        "action:n11"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the \"Items are repaired and added into inventory,\" we continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Matches the repair condition and inventory update action."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b6->n12",
        "action:n12",
        "action:n13"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "On the other hand, if the \"Items can't be repaired and are discarded,\" we email the customer with replacement charges."
      ],
      "justification": "Faithfully models the discard condition and the resulting email action."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n18",
        "guard:b12->n18"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Lastly, the items are packed for an existing order."
      ],
      "justification": "Captures the final packing step and its implicit routing condition."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b12->n19",
        "action:n19"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the \"Items are stored for future orders,\" we also continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Accurately reflects the alternative storage condition and continuation."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n20"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Once again, when the process is complete, it ends."
      ],
      "justification": "Directly implements the second stated process termination."
    }
  ],
